WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:06.320
When a movie bombs hard enough, it earns a rather&nbsp;
notorious place in the history books. As time goes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:11.760
on, the world's biggest cinematic flops come to&nbsp;
be regarded as legends — or, at the very least,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:16.400
they carry some serious name recognition. After&nbsp;
all, who doesn't remember the ridiculously&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:20.800
expensive failure that was Waterworld?&nbsp;
What about Gigli, the Ben Affleck/Jennifer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:25.760
Lopez gangster flick that was so bad it got&nbsp;
yanked out of theaters in just three weeks?

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:31.360
These films, though, are high profile failures.&nbsp;
While they certainly lost the studios some major&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:36.960
dough, they didn't set any records for being&nbsp;
the lowest grossing movie of all-time. Instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:42.720
that dubious distinction goes to a movie that —&nbsp;
fittingly enough — you've probably never heard of,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:45.760
even though it was a thriller&nbsp;
that starred two popular actors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:48.400
in Katherine Heigl and Tom Sizemore.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:54.560
Zyzzyx Road opened in U.S. theaters in February&nbsp;
of 2006. Between a weird title that Microsoft&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.560 --> 00:01:00.320
Word underlines in red, a budget of $1.2&nbsp;
million, and a bizarre release strategy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:05.040
the film earned a total gross lower than&nbsp;
your average grocery trip. Here's why.

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:10.080
First off, about the title — no, it's not&nbsp;
a typo, even though Southwest locals will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:15.920
correctly tell you that it looks an awful lot&nbsp;
like Zzyzx, which is a real place in California.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:21.040
As for some background on the film itself, since,&nbsp;
given the box office gross, you never saw it:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:25.200
it stars Leo Grillo as an accountant&nbsp;
named Grant who goes to Vegas and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:28.720
gets involved with a woman named&nbsp;
Marissa, played by Katherine Heigl.

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:33.120
They murder her ex-boyfriend, Joey, played&nbsp;
by Tom Sizemore, and cart his corpse off to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:37.920
the desert — only to find out he's still&nbsp;
alive. Zyzzyx Road was written, produced,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:43.920
and directed by John Penney, and was something&nbsp;
of a passion project. It made $30 in theaters.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:50.320
Yes, you heard right. During its entire theatrical&nbsp;
run, only six people paid money to see the film.

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:54.400
"This movie was a total disappointment. No&nbsp;
thought went into it. No effort went into it."

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:58.720
As insane as that sounds, hold your&nbsp;
laughter. Because this abysmal profit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:01.680
while it might technically&nbsp;
be the lowest gross ever,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:06.160
comes with a big asterisk — namely, that&nbsp;
nobody was supposed to buy tickets for that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:10.880
particular run of Zyzzyx Road in the first&nbsp;
place. As explained by Entertainment Weekly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:16.720
the marketing plan was to pursue international&nbsp;
sales first, then do a domestic release later on.

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:21.120
However, the name actors had accepted a lower&nbsp;
pay rate for the sake of the production,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:25.920
and the strict rules of the Screen Actor's Guild&nbsp;
required that, for them to do so, there needed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:31.440
to be a domestic release in theaters first.&nbsp;
The solution? The production rented a single&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:37.200
theater in Texas, and showed the movie only once&nbsp;
a day for six days straight. Nobody was supposed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:42.080
to know. Once the media found out, though,&nbsp;
there was no stuffing the cat back in the bag.

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:46.800
John Penney was heartbroken when the mocking&nbsp;
headlines emerged. He told Entertainment Weekly:

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:50.720
"I was mortified. [...] this movie is like&nbsp;
my baby, and it's being dragged around in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:55.600
the street with people poking sticks in it.&nbsp;
It was brutal. It was ugly. I was reeling."

00:02:55.600 --> 00:03:00.960
Embarrassing as the scenario may seem, though, the&nbsp;
notoriety helped bring attention to the film. And,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:06.240
regardless, everyone who understands the business&nbsp;
knows that the fact that it only made 30 bucks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:11.520
at the box office is really not that important.&nbsp;
Because once the film started putting out DVDs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:17.120
the international market alone&nbsp;
netted $368,000 in 23 countries.

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:20.560
Meanwhile, though, these media&nbsp;
shenanigans may have caused another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:26.000
film's reputation to get hit even harder&nbsp;
than Zyzzyx Road. In February of 2006,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:30.640
the exact same time in history where Zyzzyx&nbsp;
Road set a new low point in ticket sales,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:34.000
another thriller movie was released,&nbsp;
titled Zzyzx. What are the odds, right?

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:38.000
Zzyzx also involves murder in the&nbsp;
Southwest U.S. desert. That said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:41.040
between the similar plotlines&nbsp;
and the similar titles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:46.960
Zzyzx often gets confused with Zyzzyx Road to this&nbsp;
day. Probably for the sake of making space from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:52.320
the more well-known release, some subsequent&nbsp;
releases of Zzyxz have been retitled Burned.

